{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And not by his own power</b> — only because of the sin of Israel, for HaShem to chastise them." "<b>And he shall destroy mighty ones</b> — this is the meaning of 'it cast down to the ground from the host and from the stars and trampled them,' and he destroyed many of Israel." "<b>And even against the host of heaven he magnified himself</b> — that he is the prince of princes, who is Michael, for he is the great prince, and under him are princes. And I shall speak further about this. And he abolished the daily offering and destroyed the Temple; this is 'and the place of his sanctuary was cast down.' And do not wonder because it said it is the sanctuary of Michael, for it is the sanctuary of the honored HaShem, just as 'the Torah of Moses,' 'the staff of Elohim.'"], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:31.100884186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}